task: intent-cues-for-a-taxonomy
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-04
branch: feature/intent-cues-for-a-taxonomy
worktree: ../okay-wt-cues

why: The second of the three frictions the first caller exposed.
  `Patterns.meeting` hardcodes the canonical class names, so a caller
  with a domain-bearing taxonomy writes a mapping by hand —
  `IntentRouter.canonicalToTaxonomy` does, and its `case _ =>` sends
  every unmapped name to one class silently. A cue set should be
  stated AGAINST a `Taxon`, and renaming it onto another taxonomy
  should be total and checked.

